  C("On Scholastic realism, where does humanness exist?", ["Only in a Platonic Form", "Only in human minds", "Concretely in human beings, abstractly in finite intellects, and ultimately in the divine intellect", "Only in God, not in things"], 2, "Scholastic realism is Aristotelian in spirit: it keeps universals in things and finite minds and adds the divine intellect.", "recall"),
  C("Why is the Scholastic view not “Plato plus a God who copies the Forms”?", ["Because Scholastics deny that God exists", "Because the Forms would still be in a third realm", "Because Scholastics hold that God invented the Forms by arbitrary choice", "Because the eternal truths are God’s own understanding, not independent objects he consults"], 3, "No mindless realm remains; the truths are ideas in the divine intellect.", "analyze")
